  <style>
    :root{color-scheme:dark;--bg:#07131f;--panel:#102337;--panel2:#142b41;--line:#35526a;--text:#edf5f8;--muted:#abc1cd;--cyan:#49c7d5;--amber:#f0ad63;--green:#70d1a0;--red:#f17878;--violet:#c4a0ef;--focus:#ffd166;font:15px/1.45 Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",sans-serif}*{box-sizing:border-box}[hidden]{display:none!important}body{margin:0;background:radial-gradient(circle at 75% -15%,#173a55 0,transparent 36rem),var(--bg);color:var(--text)}header{padding:18px clamp(16px,3vw,38px);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);background:#091927ef;position:sticky;top:0;z-index:10;backdrop-filter:blur(8px)}h1{font-size:clamp(1.35rem,2.5vw,2rem);margin:0 0 3px;letter-spacing:-.025em}h2{font-size:1.08rem;margin:0 0 9px}h3{font-size:.95rem;margin:14px 0 6px}.eyebrow{text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;font-size:.72rem;color:var(--green);font-weight:750}.muted,.help{color:var(--muted)}.help{font-size:.82rem}.shell{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(280px,345px) minmax(0,1fr);gap:14px;max-width:1900px;margin:auto;padding:14px}.panel{background:linear-gradient(145deg,var(--panel2),var(--panel));border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:14px;min-width:0;box-shadow:0 10px 30px #0003}.controls{grid-row:span 12;align-self:start;position:sticky;top:101px;max-height:calc(100vh - 116px);overflow:auto}.wide{grid-column:2}.grid2{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:14px}.grid3{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:9px}.field{display:block;margin:9px 0}.field>span{display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:4px}select,input,button{font:inherit}select,input[type=range]{width:100%;background:#081a29;color:var(--text);border:1px solid #55728a;border-radius:7px;padding:7px}input[type=range]{padding:4px;accent-color:var(--cyan)}button{color:var(--text);background:#1b4967;border:1px solid #668aa0;border-radius:7px;padding:7px 10px;cursor:pointer;margin:2px}button:hover{background:#276587}button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,input:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--focus);outline-offset:2px}button:disabled,input:disabled{opacity:.48;cursor:not-allowed}.row{display:flex;gap:5px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}.spread{justify-content:space-between}.status{border-left:4px solid var(--cyan);background:#081b2a;padding:9px 10px;border-radius:5px;margin:9px 0}.warning{border-left-color:var(--amber)}.error{border-left-color:var(--red)}.badge{display:inline-block;border:1px solid #5c7b91;border-radius:99px;padding:2px 8px;font-size:.74rem;color:var(--muted);margin:2px}.badge.live{color:#07131f;background:var(--green);border-color:var(--green);font-weight:750}.snapshot{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,minmax(85px,1fr));gap:7px}.datum{background:#091c2c;border:1px solid #29465c;border-radius:8px;padding:8px;min-width:0}.datum span{color:var(--muted);font-size:.72rem;display:block;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}.datum strong{font-size:1.05rem;display:block;margin-top:2px}.stage{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-bottom:10px}.stagebox{text-align:center;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:9px;padding:10px;background:#0a1d2e}.stagebox strong{font-size:1.42rem;display:block}.arrow{text-align:center;color:var(--muted)}.irreversible{display:inline-block;color:var(--green);font-weight:750}.meter{height:7px;background:#06131f;border-radius:99px;margin-top:7px;overflow:hidden}.fill{height:100%;border-radius:99px}.plot{height:335px}.plot.big{height:470px}.plot.small{height:275px}.scroll{overflow:auto;max-height:380px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.8rem}th,td{padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid #29465c;text-align:right;white-space:nowrap}th:first-child,td:first-child{text-align:left}th{color:var(--muted);position:sticky;top:0;background:#102337}.context-json{font:12px/1.45 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;white-space:pre-wrap;background:#081a29;border-radius:7px;padding:9px;max-height:250px;overflow:auto}.hypothesis{background:#091d2d;border:1px solid #2d4b62;border-radius:9px;padding:10px;margin:7px 0}.hypothesis h3{margin:0 0 4px}.hypothesis p{margin:4px 0}.metric-note{min-height:3em}.loading{display:grid;place-items:center;min-height:100vh;padding:30px;text-align:center}.spinner{width:34px;height:34px;border:4px solid #35526a;border-top-color:var(--cyan);border-radius:50%;animation:spin .8s linear infinite;margin:12px auto}@keyframes spin{to{transform:rotate(360deg)}}details{margin-top:10px}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:700}.only-screen-reader{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;padding:0;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);white-space:nowrap;border:0}@media(max-width:1120px){.snapshot{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}}@media(max-width:900px){header{position:static}.shell{grid-template-columns:1fr}.controls{position:static;grid-row:auto;max-height:none}.wide{grid-column:1}.grid2{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:520px){.shell{padding:8px}.panel{padding:10px}.snapshot,.grid3{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.plot.big{height:390px}.stage{grid-template-columns:1fr}.irreversible{font-size:.9rem}}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div id="loading" class="loading" role="status"><div><div class="eyebrow">Offline research artifact</div><h1>Opening precomputed V5 evidence</h1><div class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></div><p class="muted">Decompressing the embedded simulation dataset locally. No network request is made.</p></div></div>
  <div id="app" hidden>
    <header>
      <div class="eyebrow">Simulation data · precomputed only · offline</div>
      <h1>Private information, adult conviction, and deference</h1>
      <div class="muted">Private ledger u and held conviction b remain distinct · ability and evidence fixed within each sweep · run <span id="runId"></span></div>
    </header>
    <main class="shell">
      <aside class="panel controls" aria-label="Dashboard controls">
        <h2>Evidence slice</h2>
        <label class="field"><span>Adult architecture</span><select id="model"></select></label>
        <label class="field"><span>Information environment</span><select id="scenario"></select></label>
        <label class="field"><span>Landscape metric</span><select id="metric"></select></label>
        <div id="metricNote" class="help metric-note"></div>
        <label class="field"><span>Deference d <output id="dOut"></output></span><input id="dSlider" type="range" min="0" max="12" step="1"></label>
        <label class="field"><span>Mean maturation time tau <output id="tauOut"></output></span><input id="tauSlider" type="range" min="0" max="14" step="1"></label>
        <div id="inactiveNote" class="status warning" hidden></div>
        <div id="selection" class="status"></div>
        <div class="row"><button id="pinSelected">Pin</button><button id="pinMatched">Pin matched set</button><button id="resetPins">Reset pins</button></div>
        <h3>Animation</h3>
        <div class="row"><button id="play">Play</button><button id="pause">Pause</button><button id="restart">Restart</button><label>Speed <select id="speed"><option value="1">1x</option><option value="2">2x</option><option value="4">4x</option></select></label></div>
        <label class="field"><span>Model time <output id="timeOut"></output></span><input id="scrub" type="range" min="0" value="0" step="1"></label>
        <h3>Exports</h3>
        <div class="row"><button id="configJson">Config JSON</button><button id="configCsv">Config CSV</button><button id="mapJson">Map JSON</button><button id="mapCsv">Map CSV</button><button id="seriesJson">Series JSON</button><button id="seriesCsv">Series CSV</button><button id="distJson">b distributions JSON</button><button id="allJson">All selected JSON</button></div>
        <details><summary>Exact context configuration</summary><pre id="configView" class="context-json"></pre></details>
        <div id="message" class="help" role="status"></div>
      </aside>

      <section class="panel wide">
        <div class="row spread"><div><h2>Selected precomputed outcome</h2><div class="help">Click a d × tau cell to load its stored trajectory. Tau is logarithmic.</div></div><span class="badge live">No live recomputation</span></div>
        <div id="traitMap" class="plot big" role="img" aria-label="Heatmap of deference by maturation time"></div>
        <div id="mapStatus" class="help"></div>
      </section>

      <section class="panel wide">
        <div class="row spread"><div><h2>Matched deference contrast</h2><div class="help">The selected cell is compared with d=0 at the same architecture, scenario, and tau. Non-reset learners on both sides retain their private ledger through maturation.</div></div><span id="matchBadge" class="badge"></span></div>
        <div class="grid2"><div id="matchedPlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Matched endpoint information measures"></div><div><div id="matchedTable" class="scroll"></div><div id="matchedNote" class="status"></div></div></div>
      </section>

      <section class="panel wide">
        <h2>State at <span id="timeLabel">t=0</span></h2>
        <div class="stage"><div class="stagebox">Juveniles F<strong id="FNow">—</strong><div class="meter"><div id="FBar" class="fill" style="background:var(--cyan)"></div></div></div><div class="arrow"><span class="irreversible">irreversible →</span><br>maturation<br><strong id="MNow">—</strong></div><div class="stagebox">Adults A<strong id="ANow">—</strong><div class="meter"><div id="ABar" class="fill" style="background:var(--amber)"></div></div></div></div>
        <div class="snapshot"><div class="datum"><span>Total N</span><strong id="NNow">—</strong></div><div class="datum"><span>Adult private u accuracy</span><strong id="privateNow">—</strong></div><div class="datum"><span>Adult held b accuracy</span><strong id="beliefNow">—</strong></div><div class="datum"><span>Teacher accuracy</span><strong id="adviceNow">—</strong></div><div class="datum"><span>Override | conflict</span><strong id="overrideNow">—</strong></div><div class="datum"><span>Query cost flow</span><strong id="queryCostNow">—</strong></div></div>
      </section>

      <section class="panel wide grid2"><div><h2>Population trajectory</h2><div id="populationPlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Juvenile adult and total population through time"></div></div><div><h2>Private ledger versus held conviction</h2><div id="ledgerPlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Private and held accuracy through time"></div></div></section>
      <section class="panel wide grid2"><div><h2>Teacher, public action, and conflict</h2><div id="behaviorPlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Teacher public action conflict and override rates through time"></div><div class="help">Conflict is P(private sign disagrees with testimony) among juveniles. Override is P(adult action chosen | disagreement); it is unavailable when conflict exposure is zero.</div></div><div><h2>Query exposure and cost</h2><div id="queryPlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Private query rates and query mortality cost through time"></div><div class="help">Rates are conditional per-capita exposure. Cost is the aggregate excess mortality flow c_query × queries and uses the right axis.</div></div></section>

      <section class="panel wide">
        <div class="row spread"><div><h2>Held-conviction score b distributions</h2><div class="help">Actual precomputed b marginals, normalized within each biological stage. b is a bounded signed conviction score, not a literal log-likelihood ratio.</div></div><span class="badge">scores −4…4</span></div>
        <div class="grid2"><div id="distFPlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Juvenile held conviction distribution through time"></div><div id="distAPlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Adult held conviction distribution through time"></div></div>
        <div id="distCursorPlot" class="plot small" role="img" aria-label="Juvenile and adult conviction distribution at selected time"></div>
      </section>

      <section class="panel wide">
        <div class="row spread"><div><h2>Pinned counterfactuals</h2><div class="help">Pins are separate precomputed cells. They do not interact and do not imply evolutionary competition.</div></div><span id="pinCount" class="badge"></span></div>
        <div class="grid2"><div id="pinPlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Pinned total population trajectories"></div><div id="pins" class="scroll"></div></div>
      </section>

      <section class="panel wide grid2"><div><h2>What changed in this scenario?</h2><div id="scenarioTable" class="scroll"></div><div id="scenarioNote" class="status warning"></div></div><div><h2>Architecture contract</h2><div id="architectureNote" class="status"></div><div id="invariants" class="context-json"></div></div></section>

      <section id="mechanismSection" class="panel wide" hidden>
        <div class="row spread"><div><h2>Acceptance versus current public override</h2><div class="help">Factorial ablation: individual learning and retention are held identical while storage acceptance and action override are independently switched.</div></div><div class="row"><label>Scenario <select id="mechScenario"></select></label><label>d <select id="mechD"></select></label><label>tau <select id="mechTau"></select></label><label>Measure <select id="mechMetric"></select></label></div></div>
        <div class="grid2"><div id="mechanismPlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Mechanism factorial comparison"></div><div><div id="mechanismTable" class="scroll"></div><div id="mechanismNote" class="status"></div></div></div>
      </section>

      <section id="sourceSection" class="panel wide" hidden>
        <div class="row spread"><div><h2>Source quality × private access</h2><div class="help">Matched d=1 minus d=0 contrast within every source condition at tau=3; this is not an across-cell causal decomposition.</div></div><div class="row"><label>Adult mode <select id="sourceMode"></select></label><label>Query cost <select id="sourceCost"></select></label><label>Measure <select id="sourceMetric"></select></label></div></div>
        <div class="grid2"><div id="sourcePlot" class="plot big" role="img" aria-label="Source quality and private access contrast heatmap"></div><div><div id="sourceTable" class="scroll"></div><div id="sourceNote" class="status warning"></div></div></div>
      </section>

      <section id="repertoireSection" class="panel wide" hidden>
        <div class="row spread"><div><h2>Independent finite-repertoire benchmark</h2><div class="help">Actual seeded simulation summary from the separate binary-fact repertoire experiment; no demography, selection, cooperation, or combinatorial reasoning.</div></div><div class="row"><label>D <select id="repD"></select></label><label>Cue p <select id="repP"></select></label><label>Environment <select id="repEnv"></select></label><label>Measure <select id="repMetric"></select></label></div></div>
        <div class="grid2"><div id="repertoirePlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Finite repertoire benchmark by deference and policy"></div><div><div id="repertoireTable" class="scroll"></div><div id="repertoireNote" class="status"></div></div></div>
      </section>

      <section id="tutorSection" class="panel wide" hidden>
        <div class="row spread"><div><h2>Observable confidence-filtered tutors</h2><div class="help">Exploratory paired filter-minus-random contrasts in the independent repertoire model. The filter sees |b|≥2, never correctness.</div></div><div class="row"><label>D <select id="tutorD"></select></label><label>Cue p <select id="tutorP"></select></label><label>Environment <select id="tutorEnv"></select></label><label>Measure <select id="tutorMetric"></select></label></div></div>
        <div class="grid2"><div id="tutorPlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Confidence-filtered tutor paired contrasts"></div><div><div id="tutorTable" class="scroll"></div><div id="tutorNote" class="status warning"></div></div></div>
      </section>

      <section id="bayesSection" class="panel wide" hidden>
        <div class="row spread"><div><h2>Exact Bayes versus bounded-score updating</h2><div class="help">Analytical one-task stable-world comparator: calibrated prior, conditionally independent cues, no social transmission, demography, or query cost.</div></div><div class="row"><label>Prior q0 <select id="bayesPrior"></select></label><label>Cue p <select id="bayesP"></select></label></div></div>
        <div class="grid2"><div id="bayesPlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Exact Bayesian and bounded score accuracy over cues"></div><div><div id="bayesTable" class="scroll"></div><div id="bayesNote" class="status warning"></div></div></div>
      </section>

      <section id="historiesSection" class="panel wide" hidden>
        <div class="row spread"><div><h2>Paired changing-history contrasts</h2><div class="help">Finite-horizon r600(d=1) − r600(d=0) on paired signed-cue histories; real truth changes and channel-only changes share event times and signed cue statistics.</div></div><div class="row"><label>Phase <select id="historyPhase"></select></label><label>Adult mode <select id="historyModel"></select></label></div></div>
        <div class="grid2"><div id="historiesPlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Paired changing history deference contrasts"></div><div><div id="historiesTable" class="scroll"></div><div id="historiesNote" class="status warning"></div></div></div>
      </section>

      <section id="selectionSection" class="panel wide" hidden>
        <div class="row spread"><div><h2>Shared-culture selection evidence</h2><div class="help">Rare-mutant architecture comparisons and explicit multi-genotype frequencies use shared adult advice and resource limitation.</div></div><div class="row"><label>Scenario <select id="selectionScenario"></select></label><label>Competition <select id="competitionKind"><option value="architectures">Architectures</option><option value="d_tau">d × tau grid</option></select></label></div></div>
        <div class="grid2"><div><h3>Mutant into resident architecture</h3><div id="architectureInvasionPlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Architecture invasion matrix"></div></div><div><h3>Actual genotype-frequency trajectory</h3><div id="competitionPlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Shared-culture genotype frequency trajectory"></div></div></div>
        <div id="selectionNote" class="status warning"></div>
        <div class="grid2"><div><h3>Refined tau candidates and mechanism invasion</h3><div id="selectionRefinementTable" class="scroll"></div><h3>Action-only versus stored copying</h3><div id="mechanismInvasionTable" class="scroll"></div><div id="selectionAddendumNote" class="help"></div></div><div><h3>Measured frozen-lineage replacement</h3><div id="replacementPlot" class="plot" role="img" aria-label="Frozen and audit lineage frequencies over long competition"></div><div id="replacementControls" class="scroll"></div><div id="replacementNote" class="status warning"></div></div></div>
      </section>

      <section id="sensitivitySection" class="panel wide grid2" hidden>
        <div><div class="row spread"><div><h2>Memory × query-cost sensitivity</h2><div class="help">Exploratory noisy-cue p=.55 matched d=1 versus d=0 rows; abundance and accuracy remain separate.</div></div><div class="row"><label>H <select id="memoryH"></select></label><label>Cost <select id="memoryCost"></select></label></div></div><div id="costMemoryTable" class="scroll"></div><div id="costMemoryNote" class="status"></div></div>
        <div><h2>Local abundance refinements</h2><div class="help">Numerical r400 abundance refinements after the coarse map; these are not evolutionary optima.</div><div id="refinementTable" class="scroll"></div><div id="convergenceNote" class="status"></div></div>
      </section>

      <section class="panel wide grid2"><div><h2>Predeclared hypotheses</h2><div id="hypotheses"></div></div><div><h2>Supplemental evidence inventory</h2><div id="supplementSummary" class="context-json"></div><h3>Dataset counts</h3><div id="counts" class="context-json"></div></div></section>

      <section class="panel wide"><details open><summary>Interpretation and hard limits</summary><p>The heatmap and trajectories are stored simulation outputs. Controls select a precomputed context or cell; the browser does not solve equations. <strong>rT</strong> and <strong>last-100-time-unit growth</strong> are finite-window population summaries. <strong>Invasion</strong> is conditional rare-mutant growth in the declared common retained resident culture and resource environment; it is not fixation probability. <strong>Survival</strong> conditions on final evidence and advice held fixed; it is not realized cohort survival through a changing environment.</p><p>For non-reset architectures, d=0 learners retain private knowledge into adulthood; they are not forced to relearn. Frozen adult conviction is an imposed no-adult-query policy, not an evolved dogmatism genotype. Confidence-based audit is also imposed and state-dependent. The oracle has privileged current reliability information and a finite-memory proxy; it is not a full Bayesian learner. The load scenario divides information exposure and does not simulate combinatorial reasoning. Source misinformation, actual signed-signal corruption, and true environmental reversal are distinct interventions. These hypothetical results do not establish human genetic separability, historical adaptation, norms, morality, or cooperation.</p></details></section>
    </main>
  </div>
